/* Learning Data: Only what you may see. The words of the series' labs (Take it apart) and scenarios (Make the call), in English.
   Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. One playground for each film, each on the chapter it plays (film, chapter), with three to
   five experiments (w.goals) the visitor ticks by making them happen; and twelve situations, the series' evaluation, each pointing to
   its playground. learn.js draws every picture from these words and keeps progress in this browser under
   "ld-only-what-you-may-see": the labs visited, the experiments ticked, and the answers by scenario number (film × 10 + its place).
   A page shows each situation's options in the order written here: the right answers are spread across the places, and the
   Spanish pack keeps them in the same places.
   build_series.py (series_learn) reads the first keys of each lab, in this order: id, kind, film, chapter, c, name; and of each
   scenario: type, n, lab, film. No other object here starts with id, and no other key is called kind or starts an object with type.
   Names and numbers follow the films' narration: Anil Kurian's study of 2,614 learners in the Faculty of Health, Mei Tanaka who owns
   the registrar's records, Yusuf Demir who keeps the agreements, agreement 2026-14 ending on 30 June 2027, the five classes and four
   levels, 163 grants on 58 tables, 140 columns on 38 tables, the teaching hospital, Elena Lindgren, the mobile column's 31 hours.
   Samuel's row and the counts by course follow Show the least. */
